  <data name="label8.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>1. Open the “Service Request Status” page
    - Click on the Service Request Status button in the side navigation
2. Check the progress of your reports
    - PENDING: your report has been submitted and will be reviewed soon
    - PROCESSING: a resolution is in progress
    - RESOLVED: the issue has been taken care of
3. Refresh button
    - If you don't see the claim you just submitted, press the refresh button</value>
  </data>
  <data name="label4.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>1. Open the “Report Issues Page”
    - Click on the Report Issues button in the side navigation
2. Enter the Location
    - Type the location of the issue (e.g., ”Main Street, near the library”)
3. Select a Category
    - Choose from the dropdown list of categories your issue falls under
4. Write a Description
    - Provide the details about the issue (e.g., “Burst water pipe causing flooding on the street”)
5. Attach Media (Optional)
    - Click the “Upload” button to add a photo or document relating to the issue
    - A file dialog will open, you can select the file you want to attach
6. Submit The Report
    - Once all the details are filled in, click the “Submit” button
    - Your report will be logged in the system</value>
  </data>
  <data name="label6.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>1. Open the “Events and Announcements” page
    - Click on the Events button in the side navigation
2. See what events are taking place in your area
    - The list shows events you can participate in
    - Dates, times, locations and details are included
3. Recommendations
    - These are the events you may be interested in based on your search history
4. FIlter and Search
    - Filter and find results for certain categories
    - Select a date to see what's happening on that date
    - Click the "Apply" button to get those events
    - Click "Clear" to show all events again
</value>
